cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use scan2beams in scholarly work, please cite it using this metadata."
title: scan2beams
abstract: "A fast C++ command-line tool for detecting and cropping long wooden beams from large 16-bit CT volumes stored as raw NRRD files. It uses sparse two-dimensional sampling and morphology, and writes cropped NRRD volumes, original-coordinate bounding boxes, and numbered diagnostic previews."
authors:
  - family-names: Huber
    given-names: Johannes A. J.
    email: johannes.huber@ltu.se
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9196-0370"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vis-florum/scan2beams"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - computed tomography
  - NRRD
  - image segmentation
  - object cropping
  - wood science
  - wooden beams
